# lec.ys -- Formal equivalence: RTL (gold) vs synthesized netlist (gate)
# Usage: yosys scripts/lec.ys   (exit code 0 = proven equivalent)
#
# v12: SMT-based temporal induction via the external yosys-smtbmc driver.
# Why: the built-in `sat -tempinduct` only supports init=0/undef/x, which
# (a) breaks FFs whose reset value is 1 (tx) and (b) puts the netlist's
# one-hot FSM into an ILLEGAL state -> false counterexample. smtbmc honors
# the (* init *) attributes that async2sync creates, so both designs start
# from their TRUE reset states. Requires: brew install z3.

read_verilog rtl/uart_tx.v
hierarchy -top uart_tx
proc
async2sync
rename uart_tx gold

read_verilog build/uart_tx_synth.v
proc
async2sync
rename uart_tx gate

flatten gold
flatten gate
miter -equiv -make_assert -make_outputs -flatten gold gate miter
smt2 -wgt build/miter.smt2
